    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d6">

                <pb facs="0020" n="10" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg10"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">846G.00/1–748: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-01-07T14:00:00+08:00">January 7, 1948—2
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 8—4:26 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>34. Embassy noticed Hong Kong dateline Story appearing in Shanghai English
                    language press January 2 of formation of “Kmt Revolutionary Committee” in Hong
                    Kong under leadership of Li Chih-Sun<anchor n="15" xml:id="d6-f1"/> and with
                    cooperation of various other prominent dissident Kmt members.</p>
                <p>Embassy would appreciate investigation and report on this development.<anchor
                        n="16" xml:id="d6-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Hong Kong 3; repeated Dept.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d6-f1" n="15" xml:id="d6-f1-content">
                <p>General Li Chi-shen was expelled from the Kuomintang in 1947 because of
                    anti-Government activities.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d6-f2" n="16" xml:id="d6-f2-content">
                <p>The Consul General at Hong Kong replied to the Ambassador in letter of January
                    17, not glinted; see unnumbered despatch of March 1 from the Consul General at
                    Hong Kong, <ref target="#pg126">p. 126</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
